 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Ibrahim, the angels, Lut and his family are never drawn: no door, no food, no figures. No plate starts on the words of Ibrahim about himself or of the angels; the only plate is geometric from «من رحمة ربه». 56 is one chip so «ومن يقنط… إلا الضالون» stays whole; 59 and 60 each keep their «إلا» with what follows. The son is named Ishaq by both tafsirs. STAGING v4: Restaged under the owner's Staging v4 decision: Ibrahim is now a blue drop labelled Ibrahim and his guests one gold angel drop labelled 'the angels' (one drop for the group: neither tafsir gives their number). Setting: his home (As-Sa'di mentions his house and the people of this house). Still never drawn: food, the calf, his wife, Lut, his family and his people; no door. The angels enter on 52:2; speak beats follow who speaks in the verses. Plates: footsteps on 52:2, a scroll on 53:5 (the good news), geometric on 56:5, light on 59:5, a seal on 60:3; no other plate is alive over the names of Ibrahim, Lut or the Lord."
 },
